    # property(fget=None, fset=None, fdel=None, doc=None)
        # PURPOSE:
            # Creates a managed attribute implemented through getter, setter, and
            # deleter methods while allowing normal attribute syntax.
        # DESCRIPTOR BEHAVIOR:
            # property is a descriptor stored on a class.
            # Reading instance.attribute can call fget(instance).
            # Assigning can call fset(instance, value).
            # Deleting can call fdel(instance).
        # COMMON DECORATOR STYLE:
            # @property defines a getter.
            # @name.setter defines a setter returning a new property object.
            # @name.deleter defines a deleter.
        # REQUIREMENTS:
            # A property must be defined on the class to participate normally in
            # instance attribute lookup.
            # A getter is needed for readable access; otherwise reading raises
            # AttributeError.
            # A setter is needed for assignment; otherwise assignment raises
            # AttributeError.
